# {{NAME}} workspace

Workspace holding the {{REPO_DIR}} repository. Everything here is planning material or worktree storage; the code lives in the repo.

## Where to work

All engineering work happens in `{{REPO_DIR}}/`. Before touching any code, read `{{REPO_DIR}}/AGENTS.md` fully and follow it: planning, workflow, commit format, tests, determinism, logging.

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `{{REPO_DIR}}/` | The repo. Start here for any code task. |
| `wt/` | Git worktrees of the repo, one per feature branch. Agents spawned into one work there; otherwise start in the repo. |

## Order of truth

1. User instruction in the current session.
2. `{{REPO_DIR}}/STATE.md` for live repo state.
3. `{{REPO_DIR}}/AGENTS.md` for rules and workflow.
4. This file's plan notes, if any, for workspace-level strategy.

## Skills

- Repo skills: `{{REPO_DIR}}/.agents/skills/` (canonical for repo work).
- Global skills: `~/.agents/skills/` (all projects). When the same skill exists in both, the repo copy wins for repo work; edit it in the repo.
